<head>
    <title>Interactive Markdown</title>
    <meta name="description" content="HTMX-powered interactivity inside a Markdown body — components, styles, and scripts coexist.">
</head>

<server>
    siteName := "Dreego"
    featureCount := 3
</server>

<style>
.interactive-note {
    border-left: 4px solid #0f766e;
    background: #f0fdfa;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: #134e4a;
}
.interactive-note strong {
    color: #0f766e;
}
</style>

<client>
console.log("interactive post loaded");
</client>

<body lang="md">
# Interactive Markdown

This post shows how a Markdown body can host real interactivity. Alongside the prose, a scoped style section styles a callout box, a client section runs an inline script, and raw HTML with HTMX attributes lives right inside the Markdown.

## What coexists here

About {{ siteName }}, this page proves that a Markdown body is not limited to static text. It combines three verified features in one document:

- A scoped style section that styles the callout below
- A client section that logs to the browser console
- Raw HTML with HTMX attributes embedded in the prose

## The callout

> **Scoped styles work.** This box is styled by the route's own style section, scoped to this page and coexisting with the Markdown body.

## Try it

The button below is raw HTML rendered inside the Markdown. It carries HTMX attributes, so clicking it fetches the blog index and swaps it into the main content area.

<a href="/blog/" hx-get="/blog/" hx-target="#main" hx-swap="outerHTML" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-slate-950 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-700">Load more posts</a>

## What this proves

There are {{ featureCount }} verified capabilities demonstrated on this page. Raw HTML, styles, and scripts all survive generation inside a Markdown body.

## Verified features

| Feature | Status | Since |
| --- | :---: | --- |
| Scoped styles | Done | v0.3 |
| Client scripts | Done | v0.3 |
| Raw HTML + HTMX | Done | v0.3 |
| Pipe tables | Done | v0.3 |

![Dreego logo](https://dreego.dev/logo.svg)

## Nested lists

- Markdown blocks
  - Paragraphs and headings
  - Lists and blockquotes
- Inline formatting
  - Emphasis and strong
  - Code and links

## Footnotes

Dreego[^1] renders Markdown to HTML at generation time.

[^1]: Dreego is a compile-time Go web framework.

## Keep reading

Back to the [blog index](/blog/), or see the [Markdown in the Body](/blog/posts/markdown-in-the-body) post for the base feature.
</body>
